USOS 3.1.2-usos6 patch 7/7 (2026-10-14): ACPI mode enabled before the legacy boot (diagnostic, Windows 2000 ACPI flow only)

Windows 2000's acpi.sys switches the machine from legacy to ACPI mode
itself: when PM1a_CNT.SCI_EN is 0 it writes FADT.ACPI_ENABLE to
FADT.SMI_CMD and polls SCI_EN; when SCI_EN is already 1 it sends no SMI.
On the X470 (AMI) the 2000 ACPI HAL's RTC IRQ 8 clock stops after kernel
phase 1; one hypothesis (outside review of the SP4 binaries, 2026-10-14)
is that the firmware's ACPI-enable SMI changes RTC/FCH state. This patch
lets CSMWrap do the legacy to ACPI transition the way the ACPI
specification describes it (6.5: 4.8.2.1 SCI_EN, 5.2.9 SMI_CMD /
ACPI_ENABLE / PM1a_CNT_BLK / PM_TMR_BLK, 16.3.1) as the last step before
Legacy16Boot, after SeaBIOS's PrepareToBoot has programmed the RTC, and
records the RTC status registers A and B around it:

  - only with csmwrap.ini acpi_legacy_fadt = true (written by
    tools/xp_csmwrap_esp.sh only for Windows 2000 with ACPI); every other
    flow runs the same code path as 3.1.2-usos5;
  - the FADT is the one the RSDT lists (the ACPI 1.0 copy patch 0006
    gives 2000), read before ExitBootServices: SMI_CMD, ACPI_ENABLE,
    PM1a_CNT_BLK and PM_TMR_BLK (32-bit fields, else X_ GAS in System
    I/O), Flags TMR_VAL_EXT / HW_REDUCED_ACPI;
  - RTC A/B read through index 70h with the NMI-disable bit (register C
    is never read); SCI_EN 1 -> 'a'; else out SMI_CMD, ACPI_ENABLE and
    SCI_EN polled for at most 3 s on the PM timer (8,000,000 polls cap)
    -> 'o' / 't'; no usable fields -> 'n';
  - result in the BIOS data area's inter-application communication area,
    physical 0x4F4-0x4FB (SeaBIOS leaves 0x4F0-0x4FF alone; 0x4F0-0x4F3
    are the USOS MBR's slots): 'A' 'E' status, RTC A before, RTC A after,
    RTC B before, RTC B after, PM1a_CNT low byte after; 's' is stored
    before the SMI (a machine that never returns from it keeps 's'); the
    store goes through the firmware's identity page tables with CR0.WP
    cleared and the entry for VA 0 made present for the store only;
  - logged as "USOS ACPIEN: ..." (the result line goes to serial only:
    SeaBIOS owns the screen by then).

SeaBIOS can still change RTC B after this point: INT 15h AH=83h/86h and
its thread preemption toggle the periodic-interrupt bit (rtc_use /
rtc_release), and INT 1Ah AH=03h/05h/06h/07h rewrite B. The Windows 2000
HAL programs A and B itself in HAL phase 1.

New src/usos_acpien.c (own code, no EFI dependency: port I/O through ops,
host unit test tools/tests/csmwrap/test_csmwrap_acpien.py),
src/usos_acpien.h, src/usos_acpien_efi.c (glue). Applies to CSMWrap 3.1.2
(808ac8e) with its seabios submodule (578d260b) after patches 0001-0006,
patch -p1 from the top of the tree. Part of CSMWrap 3.1.2-usos6, a
MODIFIED version made by the USOS project (LGPL-2.1 / SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

